            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "BPRWATSON"
            },
            "reviewBody": "i love honey mustard dressing but wanted a healthier version so i used plain fat free yogurt instead of mayo. Also it was a little sweet for me so i just added more mustard to taste and added a dash of pepper for some kick. It was great, Couldn't tell it wasn't made with mayo even DH liked it and he hates anything low-fat."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "WhirledPeas"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was very a very good (and simple!) dressing to make. The only thing I did differently was to use honey dijon stone ground mustard. I have also previously tried the dressing with the regualar mustard, but my family and I prefer the dijon. Thanks!",
            "datePublished": "2002-09-05T01:53:04.467Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SpryBacon6829"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added 1/2 - 1 tbs balsamic vinegar for a little punch. It's now a family favorite.",
            "datePublished": "2024-03-01T07:09:03.905Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ChelleTackett"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Like other reviewers, I changed the ratio of Mayo to honey, and mustard. I used 1/4 cup mayo, 4 tbs honey, 4 tbs horseradish mustard (like a grainy mustard), and 2 tbs lemon. Holy Moses! Turns out just like a restaurant version! Yummo!",
            "datePublished": "2017-10-09T18:47:06.100Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lemonsnax"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I quadrupled the recipe; added 2 tbsp of vinegar, 1 tbsp chopped dill, and 1/4 tsp of pepper and it made a wonderful pasta salad dressing!",
            "datePublished": "2017-04-05T23:59:11.733Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jane"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Honey Mustard and Vidalia Onion are my two favorite dressings. For this Honey Mustard recipe, I tweaked it to suit my own tastes. 8 oz. Mustard to 16 oz. Lite Mayo, 3 Tbl Apple Cider Vinegar, 4 packs of no-calorie sweetener. Fewer calories than I would normally buy in the store, and the mustard flavor is more prominent.",
            "datePublished": "2017-08-10T16:06:07.480Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Nadia"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I thought it was good. I also added a sprinkling of salt, pepper and garlic powder based on a previous review. The garlic did it for me. Next time, I may use a tad less mayo because I could distinctly taste it. (I used Dukes, which is milder than Hellmans and not as sweet as Miracle Whip.) I probably could also decrease the honey a little, but the recipe as is was delicious. Make it, then tweek to your preference. 😁",
            "datePublished": "2023-07-12T13:48:21.357Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "stephanie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've tried to find the right recipe for honey mustard dressing for years, but none were ever anything worth making, and it always seemed like something was missing but I couldn't put my finger on it--turns out it was lemon juice missing. I made two batches of this version today, one using spicy brown and the other dijon. They are both delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2020-01-31T00:19:11.017Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Melissa Anderson"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Perfect as written! For an Indian-style twist, add 1.5 tbsp cumin and 1 tbsp curry powder per cup of dressing.",
            "datePublished": "2016-09-12T19:36:52.583Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "juicedharp"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This dressing is so delicious that during dinner I got up and made more. In fact, I ended up tripling the recipe and there were no leftovers. I recommend doubling the recipe if you're cooking for two. My friend was amazed. She say's she payed more than four dollars for a small bottle of honey mustard mayo and it wasn't nearly as good as this. \nI made it again to serve with fillet of sole. This time I added a tsp of curry powder. OMG!! It was sooooo good!",
            "datePublished": "2018-08-31T02:25:54.440Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ms Jean"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent! I followed the recommendation of others and used Dijon mustard. I only added a little black pepper. Had it over a salad, and it was delicious. I doubled the recipe so I'd have some for a few more salads, or even chicken nuggets. Homemade dressings are so much better and healthier than the store-bought one! Thanks for this easy and delicious recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2017-04-24T21:51:39.243Z"
          },
          {
